  "id": "in-situ-hybridization",
  "term": "in situ hybridization",
  "definition": "In situ hybridization is a method for marking specific DNA sequences within chromatin so their locations can be seen with imaging techniques, often by fluorescence labeling. The packet describes it as a common way to visualize particular genetic loci in cells, while noting that some preparation steps can alter native chromatin structure.",
